WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:02.101
(hip-hop music)

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:04.384
- [Zipporah] People say
that, like, “Oh, like we're doin' this

00:00:04.384 --> 00:00:06.184
“because black girls can't do ballet,

00:00:06.184 --> 00:00:07.733
“so this is their alternative.”

00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:09.181
It has nothin' to do with that.

00:00:09.181 --> 00:00:10.915
I will tell you, every girl in this studio

00:00:10.915 --> 00:00:12.881
is classically trained. (laughing)

00:00:12.881 --> 00:00:16.075
Everyone does ballet, and everything else.

00:00:16.075 --> 00:00:18.742
(hip-hop music)

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:21.703
- [Homer] Last one.

00:00:21.703 --> 00:00:22.976
And down.

00:00:22.976 --> 00:00:24.126
Heels.

00:00:24.126 --> 00:00:26.035
Bounce, bounce.

00:00:26.035 --> 00:00:26.934
Bounce.

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:29.493
- My name is Zipporah Wilson,
and I'm a hiplet dancer.

00:00:29.493 --> 00:00:31.654
Hiplet is a mixture of hip-hop and ballet

00:00:31.654 --> 00:00:34.296
but really anything that
we can try to put en pointe

00:00:34.296 --> 00:00:37.145
that has like a groovy feeling to it.

00:00:37.145 --> 00:00:38.365
- My name is Homer Hans Bryant,

00:00:38.365 --> 00:00:41.496
and I'm the founder of hiplet,
and the founder and director

00:00:41.496 --> 00:00:44.088
of the Chicago Multicultural Dance Center.

00:00:44.088 --> 00:00:48.117
I think some people get mad
when they see us doing hiplet.

00:00:48.117 --> 00:00:50.214
It's not traditional classical ballet.

00:00:50.214 --> 00:00:51.475
We're ruinin' ballet.

00:00:51.475 --> 00:00:53.517
Well no, it's not ballet, it's hiplet.

00:00:53.517 --> 00:00:55.835
It's how we empower our kids,

00:00:55.835 --> 00:00:58.296
it's how we empower the world.

00:00:58.296 --> 00:01:01.373
Hiplet is so freein' and so open.

00:01:01.373 --> 00:01:04.128
There's a different culture here.

00:01:04.128 --> 00:01:06.917
- Some of the hiplet movements
are the hiplet strut,

00:01:06.917 --> 00:01:08.517
the twist in and out,

00:01:08.517 --> 00:01:09.600
the moonwalk,

00:01:10.859 --> 00:01:12.107
the vivian,

00:01:12.107 --> 00:01:13.274
and the zippy.

00:01:15.099 --> 00:01:16.368
You have to have a certain posture

00:01:16.368 --> 00:01:17.956
when you're doing ballet.

00:01:17.956 --> 00:01:21.196
Usually you're up tall, like straight figure,

00:01:21.196 --> 00:01:22.688
posture, everything.

00:01:22.688 --> 00:01:24.467
Pointe shoes were designed for ballet.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:25.824
Hiplet is different.

00:01:25.824 --> 00:01:28.633
In hiplet, you can break that,
you can just really move

00:01:28.633 --> 00:01:30.816
your torso more, and you can bounce with it.

00:01:30.816 --> 00:01:32.896
You know, you can have fun with it.

00:01:32.896 --> 00:01:34.520
- You got it, you got it!

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.156
- I grew up thinking
that I couldn't do ballet

00:01:37.156 --> 00:01:38.804
because of the color of my skin.

00:01:38.804 --> 00:01:41.254
At my old studio, because
I was African-American

00:01:41.254 --> 00:01:42.994
I was often overlooked.

00:01:42.994 --> 00:01:45.213
Until I came to CMDC is
when I really learned

00:01:45.213 --> 00:01:47.332
that there was somethin' off.

00:01:47.332 --> 00:01:49.488
I'm grateful to Mr. Homer
because he's shown me

00:01:49.488 --> 00:01:51.933
that I can do anything.

00:01:51.933 --> 00:01:53.929
I love dancing hiplet.

00:01:53.929 --> 00:01:55.828
It just gives you a sort of a confidence

00:01:55.828 --> 00:01:59.577
and just a freedom of
just, to be yourself.

00:01:59.577 --> 00:02:03.463
This is the dance genre
that does not discriminate.

00:02:03.463 --> 00:02:05.238
If you have rhythm, and
you can groove en pointe,

00:02:05.238 --> 00:02:06.250
you got it.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.917
(hip-hop music)

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.797
(electronic music)

